Z||000000||CC Rider||05-04-2001||11:58 AM||||One quick question about touch up paint. I Have a 87 GT ( Red ) and need to clean up the paint a bit but I'm having trouble finding the little bottles of paint, with the brush, for the main body and the silver gray lower trim. My GM paint code is 77 ( Med. Red Met. ) and the sticker code is WA-9077. Duplicolor and Plasti-kote do not list either of these numbers and I've tried doing a visual match up with no luck - Help Please !||||reg||6
Z||000001||Carrolles||05-04-2001||12:14 PM||||Short of getting paint mixed I think FOCOA is the only place to get original color touch up paint.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-04-2001||12:25 PM||||if you cant find the bottles in parts store, your going to have to go to auto paint store. most only sell a full pint or larger. So its kinda pricy, around $35 @ pint. Sherwin Williams will usually mix a half pint of acrylic enamel. I use ICI (division of PPG) they sell 1/4, 1/2 pints. might check to see if theres an ICI Autocolor in your yellow pages under 'Body Shop Supplies' from them, its around $10 @ 1/4 pint.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||CC Rider||09-18-2001||04:17 PM||||Found this link today and passing it along to help others with hard to find Touch Up Paint. A little spendy but you can get it in touch up bottles or spray cans<BR> <A HREF="http://www.paintscratch.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paintscratch.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||09-18-2001||10:08 PM||||CC Rider,thanks for the info on the touch up paint supplier.  I too have an 87 with the Med red code 77 which wasn't listed in the 41 colors for 87 Pontiacs.  I e-mailed them for some clarification.  I have a FOCOA touch up bottle, but need some method for spray painting a small area. We will see if they have it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||CC Rider||09-19-2001||11:47 AM||||Lower Boby Color for 1987 Pontiac All Models<BR>Medium Gray Metallic Clearcoat  18/WA7719<P>I'm sending this so it will be in the archive for other to find if needed||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||09-19-2001||11:56 AM||||You can thin it and spray it with a hobby airbrush. Also auto paint stores have a disposable sprayer with a freon can to spray small areas. I think there about $10.00||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||09-19-2001||07:57 PM||||I received e-mail that the 1987 Med Red Metallic Clear coat is 77/wa9077.<P>I'll have to get me a can of the spray paint.<P>Again..Thanks for the source!!||||reg||1
